# Re-request Copilot review after addressing review comments

When watching a PR via `subscribe_pr_activity` and you push a commit in
response to Copilot's review comments, also re-request review from Copilot
so it re-evaluates the new commit. The auto-merge workflow in
`.github/workflows/copilot-review.yml` only fires on `pull_request`
(opened/ready_for_review) and `pull_request_review` events — a plain
push won't trigger Copilot. Without an explicit re-request, the loop
stalls.

## How

Prefer the GitHub MCP tool if available:

- `mcp__github__request_copilot_review` (owner, repo, pullNumber)

Otherwise call GraphQL directly (same approach the workflow uses):

```bash
copilot_id=$(gh api graphql -F owner="$OWNER" -F name="$NAME" -f query='
  query($owner: String!, $name: String!) {
    repository(owner: $owner, name: $name) {
      suggestedActors(capabilities: [CAN_BE_ASSIGNED], first: 100) {
        nodes { login ... on Bot { id } ... on User { id } }
      }
    }
  }
' --jq '[.data.repository.suggestedActors.nodes[] | select(.login | IN("Copilot","Copilot[bot]","copilot-pull-request-reviewer","copilot-pull-request-reviewer[bot]")) | .id] | first // ""')

gh api graphql -F pullRequestId="$PR_NODE_ID" -F userId="$copilot_id" -f query='
  mutation($pullRequestId: ID!, $userId: ID!) {
    requestReviews(input: {pullRequestId: $pullRequestId, userIds: [$userId]}) {
      pullRequest { id }
    }
  }
'
```

## When NOT to re-request

- The user told you to stop, unsubscribe, or merge as-is.
- The push wasn't a response to Copilot feedback (unrelated work, manual
  fix from the user, etc.).
- The PR is already merged or closed.
- Copilot isn't available on the repo (empty `copilot_id`) — surface a
  one-line warning to the user instead of looping.

## Cap the loop

If Copilot keeps surfacing trivial nits across 3+ rounds with no
substantive improvement, stop re-requesting and summarize the remaining
suggestions to the user. Don't spin on stylistic preferences forever.
